Abraham.

00:47:46.580 --> 00:47:53.140
When someone told him General Grant was drinking every night,

00:47:53.160 --> 00:47:58.970
he answered, go on out, see if you can't get all my generals tired.

00:48:00.380 --> 00:48:05.700
That's why we celebrate this blessed February day.

00:48:06.180 --> 00:48:10.560
Abraham, Abraham, Abraham.

00:48:32.300 --> 00:48:33.780
I give up. She's not here tonight.

00:48:35.860 --> 00:48:37.440
You wait here. I'll go up and see if Jim's seen her.

00:48:38.550 --> 00:48:40.170
Gus is waiting to take you to the station.

00:48:40.330 --> 00:48:41.550
Remember now, day after tomorrow.

00:48:41.690 --> 00:48:42.610
St. Valentine's Day.

00:48:46.220 --> 00:48:47.800
Someone's coming. We better use the other stairway.

00:48:47.860 --> 00:48:48.400
Who is it?

00:48:48.500 --> 00:48:49.040
Bill collector.

00:49:01.850 --> 00:49:02.210
Good night.

00:49:02.570 --> 00:49:03.290
Good night, Jim.

00:49:04.230 --> 00:49:06.290
You better get inside before you catch cold.

00:49:06.470 --> 00:49:07.330
You haven't got a coat.

00:49:08.360 --> 00:49:09.040
Well, I...

00:49:09.040 --> 00:49:09.640
Go on.

00:49:14.300 --> 00:49:15.160
Don't need a coat now.

00:49:18.510 --> 00:49:19.010
Hey, Ted.

00:49:20.330 --> 00:49:20.970
Did you find the girl?

00:49:21.450 --> 00:49:22.170
This is terrible.

00:49:22.430 --> 00:49:23.850
I wish we could recognize her from the front.

00:49:24.120 --> 00:49:25.040
I feel like a wolf.

00:49:25.580 --> 00:49:25.980
By Ted.

00:49:43.340 --> 00:49:45.040
I saw him. This way.

00:49:45.180 --> 00:49:47.780
This way. Shortcut. Shortcut. Come on.

00:49:48.680 --> 00:49:56.730
Here. It's locked.

00:49:56.930 --> 00:49:57.950
It's never been locked before.

00:49:58.290 --> 00:49:59.450
Let's try the other stairway.

00:50:02.520 --> 00:50:12.250
Well, we've lost her again. Did you get a look at her face this time?

00:50:13.300 --> 00:50:15.580
No, we're still working from the rear.

00:50:16.140 --> 00:50:18.200
How do you know it was her? After all, she had an overcoat on.

00:50:18.420 --> 00:50:22.320
I don't care if she had... How do you know she had an overcoat on?

00:50:22.900 --> 00:50:26.430
Well, she... If she didn't, look for a girl with pneumonia.

00:50:26.830 --> 00:50:27.610
Come on, let's get inside.

00:50:30.250 --> 00:50:32.370
Say, Jim, when's your next show?

00:50:32.740 --> 00:50:33.280
Next show?

00:50:34.060 --> 00:50:35.520
St. Valentine's Day, I think.

00:50:36.330 --> 00:50:37.510
Oh, day after tomorrow, huh?

00:50:37.690 --> 00:50:38.030
Is it?

00:50:38.290 --> 00:50:38.950
That's a great.

00:50:39.090 --> 00:50:41.250
We'll get here bright and early and stay until we find her.

00:50:41.370 --> 00:50:43.470
And we'll make an announcement asking her to identify herself.

00:50:43.840 --> 00:50:45.020
We won't miss next time.

00:50:45.600 --> 00:50:47.200
Say, fellas, how'd you like the show?

00:50:47.960 --> 00:50:50.520
Well, we were so busy, we didn't see much of it, Jim.

00:50:51.160 --> 00:50:51.520
Why?

00:50:52.190 --> 00:50:54.270
Thought the people seemed to like the blackface routine.

00:50:54.840 --> 00:50:55.400
Yeah, they did.

00:50:55.840 --> 00:50:58.580
Don't you think a blackface number on St. Valentine's Day would be novel?

00:50:59.370 --> 00:50:59.710
A what?

00:51:00.380 --> 00:51:02.650
It's no good, huh? Just an idea I had.

00:51:02.980 --> 00:51:03.800
Well, goodbye.

00:51:04.230 --> 00:51:04.850
Goodbye, Ted.

00:51:04.950 --> 00:51:05.730
So long, Jim.

00:51:05.890 --> 00:51:06.250
Bye, Dad.

00:51:20.810 --> 00:51:23.270
You know, we open in an hour, and you haven't even had a rehearsal.

00:51:27.550 --> 00:51:28.250
Very smart.

00:51:28.870 --> 00:51:29.970
You'll have to talk Gus into...

00:51:31.100 --> 00:51:33.540
I spent half my life between here and the station.

00:51:34.760 --> 00:51:37.320
Gus will have to face the machine age sooner or later, won't he?

00:51:40.140 --> 00:51:41.920
Did you escape those bill collectors the other night?

00:51:41.940 --> 00:51:43.970
Bill collectors? Oh, yes, temporarily.

00:51:44.090 --> 00:51:45.810
So that reminds me, I got a surprise for you downstairs.

00:51:46.150 --> 00:51:47.930
Well, thanks. What reminds you?

00:51:48.280 --> 00:51:51.260
Nothing. It's just, I mean, I want you to remember the surprise

00:51:51.260 --> 00:51:53.200
when those doggone bill collectors move in.

00:51:53.940 --> 00:51:55.860
You sound sweet, but you don't make sense.

00:52:03.290 --> 00:52:04.990
Inn is so romantic-looking.

00:52:05.170 --> 00:52:07.400
Nice. I posed for those cupids myself.

00:52:09.200 --> 00:52:09.900
Hello, boys.

00:52:10.340 --> 00:52:11.380
Hi, Union.

00:52:12.320 --> 00:52:13.720
Paid up cards here tonight.

00:52:14.580 --> 00:52:15.680
Where's the prize?

00:52:16.370 --> 00:52:19.370
Ah, right here. A little home cooking I whipped up.

00:52:30.090 --> 00:52:31.550
Be careful, it's my heart.

00:52:32.210 --> 00:52:33.210
No, I ain't kidding, ain't I?

00:52:33.800 --> 00:52:35.020
I wrote this just for you, honey.

00:52:45.400 --> 00:52:48.610
Careful, my heart.

00:52:51.680 --> 00:52:52.900
It's not my watch.

00:52:53.140 --> 00:52:54.080
You're holding.

00:52:54.440 --> 00:52:55.800
It's my heart.

00:52:58.320 --> 00:52:59.700
It's not the nose.

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:02.560
I sent you that you

00:53:02.560 --> 00:53:04.310
quickly burned.

00:53:04.950 --> 00:53:07.500
It's not the book I lent

00:53:07.500 --> 00:53:09.350
you that you

00:53:09.350 --> 00:53:11.110
never returned.

00:53:12.390 --> 00:53:13.070
Remember.

00:53:15.730 --> 00:53:23.380
It's my heart, the heart with which so willingly I part.

00:53:24.580 --> 00:53:29.780
It's yours to take, to keep or break.

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:38.960
But please, before you start, be careful, it's my heart.

00:53:50.550 --> 00:53:59.450
Careful, it's my heart.

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:05.300
It's not my watch you're holding, it's my heart.

00:54:07.920 --> 00:54:14.140
It's not the note I sent you that you quickly burned.

00:54:15.540 --> 00:54:21.820
It's not the book I lent you that you never returned.

00:54:25.360 --> 00:54:28.570
Remember, it's my heart.

00:54:31.980 --> 00:54:36.280
The heart with which so willingly I power.

00:54:39.084 --> 00:54:40.824
It's yours to take.

00:54:41.200 --> 00:54:42.460
To keep our brave.

00:54:42.892 --> 00:54:46.652
But please, before you start...

00:54:47.916 --> 00:54:48.516
Careful.

00:54:50.156 --> 00:54:51.936
It's my heart.

00:56:10.560 --> 00:56:14.760
jim i couldn't resist it wonderful she's perfect light as a feather you found her

00:56:15.000 --> 00:56:15.540
You're a pal.

00:56:15.820 --> 00:56:16.060
Yeah.

00:56:16.380 --> 00:56:19.380
Young lady, do you realize that we've been searching for you for weeks?

00:56:19.540 --> 00:56:20.090
For me?

00:56:20.210 --> 00:56:24.400
Yes, ever since the girl in the flower shop.

00:56:24.740 --> 00:56:25.580
Yes, Mr. Reed.

00:56:26.440 --> 00:56:28.020
Where have you been working since New Year's Eve?

00:56:28.400 --> 00:56:28.620
Here.

00:56:30.572 --> 00:56:32.572
Would you mind letting me in on your secret?

00:56:32.624 --> 00:56:33.404
Oh, it's no secret.

00:56:33.868 --> 00:56:36.968
Ted Hanover's looking for a new dancing partner, and we've decided to give you the job.

00:56:37.028 --> 00:56:38.468
Oh, here, now, wait. Wait just a minute.

00:56:38.508 --> 00:56:40.748
Oh, no hard feelings, Jim. I don't blame you for trying.

00:56:40.928 --> 00:56:43.388
She's wonderful. I feel as if I'd known her for months.

00:56:43.528 --> 00:56:44.868
Oh, same old feeling, huh?

00:56:45.580 --> 00:56:47.840
Let's see, Washington's birthday is the next show.

00:56:48.236 --> 00:56:49.496
That'll give us a week of rehearsals.

00:56:49.712 --> 00:56:50.812
We can open the act here.

00:56:50.952 --> 00:56:52.032
I'll take care of the invitations.

00:56:52.396 --> 00:56:56.636
strictly formal i'll get all the newspaper boys from new york now hold everything this is my

00:56:56.636 --> 00:56:59.036
in and i'm not running it for a bunch of stuffed shirts

00:56:59.308 --> 00:56:59.968
What would you like?

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:00.660
The dungaree set?

00:57:00.940 --> 00:57:03.140
Well, that'll be better than that bunch of chowder heads you'd drag in.

00:57:03.280 --> 00:57:04.820
Maybe I can't use the act.

00:57:05.230 --> 00:57:06.690
Not use Ted Hanover?

00:57:06.790 --> 00:57:08.360
Well, the show's pretty well set.

00:57:08.580 --> 00:57:10.450
You're in, but he's out.

00:57:10.840 --> 00:57:13.680
But you could change the show for a special occasion like this.

00:57:13.840 --> 00:57:14.720
Of course he could.

00:57:15.000 --> 00:57:16.260
He's just trying to hide his gratitude.

00:57:16.760 --> 00:57:18.440
Jim, you better think up a number for us.

00:57:19.060 --> 00:57:21.340
Well, just what do you visualize, Ziggy?

00:57:21.480 --> 00:57:23.240
Uh, let's see.

00:57:24.020 --> 00:57:27.750
For Washington's birthday, I see a sort of a romantic costume thing.

00:57:27.950 --> 00:57:28.330
Naturally.

00:57:28.570 --> 00:57:29.850
Something that just reeks.

00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:31.800
with grace and charm, you know?

00:57:31.884 --> 00:57:33.344
I think the music should be sweet.

00:57:33.804 --> 00:57:35.484
gentle to, well, to...

00:57:35.564 --> 00:57:38.504
create the mood each time I take her into my arms and kiss her.

00:57:39.820 --> 00:57:40.820
That's it.

00:57:41.004 --> 00:57:42.844
Don't you think it's getting a little stuffy in here?

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:29.980
