00:58:34.284 --> 00:58:36.564
I could say that you're homely.

00:58:37.420 --> 00:58:39.480
Just as homely as pie.

00:58:40.140 --> 00:58:47.300
But this is Washington's birthday, and I've got to say, you're beautiful cause I can.

00:58:47.628 --> 00:58:48.828
Tell a lie.

00:58:49.868 --> 00:58:51.828
I could say that you're stupid.

00:58:52.876 --> 00:58:55.056
Nothing up in your crown.

00:58:55.948 --> 00:58:58.148
But this is Washington's birthday.

00:58:58.640 --> 00:59:00.000
And the Truthful He-

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:01.580
of the cherry tree

00:59:01.580 --> 00:59:03.300
would look down on me

00:59:03.300 --> 00:59:04.880
and frown.

00:59:05.372 --> 00:59:07.612
I could say that I hate you.

00:59:07.996 --> 00:59:09.136
If I try.

00:59:11.036 --> 00:59:13.696
But I've got to say, I love you.

00:59:14.076 --> 00:59:19.876
Cause it's February the 22nd and I can't tell a lie.

01:02:10.300 --> 01:02:13.860
Well, honey, in spite of what good old Jim tried to do to us, your future starts as of tonight.

01:02:14.570 --> 01:02:15.810
Now, where would you like to go from here?

01:02:16.660 --> 01:02:17.140
From here?

01:02:17.550 --> 01:02:20.890
Yes, New York, Havana, Rio. We have our pick of engagements, you know.

01:02:21.260 --> 01:02:23.160
But I can't be your partner if you leave the inn.

01:02:23.720 --> 01:02:26.370
Of course you can. There's no reason for you to remain buried here.

01:02:27.930 --> 01:02:28.990
There's a very good reason.

01:02:30.220 --> 01:02:33.400
I've promised to be in Jim's holiday shows for the rest of the year.

01:02:33.710 --> 01:02:35.930
Oh, but he tricked you into that while he was hiding you from me.

01:02:36.560 --> 01:02:38.460
No matter how he did it, I've promised.

01:02:40.080 --> 01:02:43.300
Besides, we're, well, we're going to be married.

01:02:43.610 --> 01:02:43.970
Married?

01:02:44.600 --> 01:02:45.400
Well, now, wait a minute.

01:02:45.600 --> 01:02:46.400
Let's be fair.

01:02:46.890 --> 01:02:48.050
He didn't give me a chance.

01:02:48.270 --> 01:02:49.490
After all, I love you, too.

01:02:50.820 --> 01:02:52.600
Linda, from the very first moment we danced together,

01:02:52.840 --> 01:02:54.640
I knew you were to be the one girl in my life.

01:02:55.280 --> 01:02:56.940
You didn't even know my name.

01:02:58.350 --> 01:02:58.710
Please.

01:02:59.790 --> 01:02:59.970
All right.

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:03.370
Forget about me, then. Forget about Jim. Think of yourself.

01:03:03.950 --> 01:03:05.770
Here's your chance to do the one thing you like best.

01:03:06.160 --> 01:03:08.280
Not only for 15 days a year, but always.

01:03:11.240 --> 01:03:13.070
Sorry, but I promised.

01:03:13.390 --> 01:03:29.160
I guess I should apologize for hooking up your number, huh?

01:03:29.480 --> 01:03:29.960
Oh, forget it.

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:32.740
I'm the one that should apologize to you.

01:03:33.980 --> 01:03:37.140
Here I've been trying to take Linda away from you, not knowing you two are going to be married.

01:03:37.660 --> 01:03:38.020
Married?

01:03:39.610 --> 01:03:41.460
Yeah. Aren't you?

01:03:43.080 --> 01:03:47.810
Yes. Sure. I mean, naturally, we're sort of engaged.

01:03:48.970 --> 01:03:54.550
Oh. Well, anyway, I've decided to bow out of here. Linda's all yours.

01:03:55.360 --> 01:03:57.460
Well, you're a pretty game guy to take it this way.

01:03:57.920 --> 01:03:59.840
It's happened so often I'm getting used to it, that's all.

01:04:01.600 --> 01:04:02.020
Goodbye, kid.

01:04:02.560 --> 01:04:03.240
Out of luck, Dad.

01:04:04.200 --> 01:04:04.440
Thanks.

01:04:04.660 --> 01:04:13.450
What are we doing?

01:04:14.620 --> 01:04:17.080
Two minutes ago, I would have sold my chances for a tired dime.

01:04:17.240 --> 01:04:19.440
But when a man is surprised to hear that he's going to be married,

01:04:19.850 --> 01:04:21.930
brother, that's when I go to work with a clear conscience.

01:04:22.840 --> 01:04:23.540
Everything's good, huh?

01:04:23.600 --> 01:04:24.400
Everything is perfect.

01:05:04.980 --> 01:05:19.700
Mr. Bonnet, with all the thrills upon it, you'll be the grandest lady in the Easter Parade.

01:05:21.400 --> 01:05:29.980
I'll be all in clover, and when they look you over, I'll be the proudest.

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:55.840
The proudest fella in the Easter parade on the avenue, fifth avenue, the photographers will snap us and you'll find that you're in the road to grab your own eyes.

01:05:56.630 --> 01:05:59.830
Write a sonnet about.

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:29.980
Out your Easter bonnet, and of the girl I'm taking, to the Easter parade, on the Avenue, Fifth Avenue, the photographers will snap us, and you'll find that you're, in the road to gravure, oh.

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:38.470
Write a sonnet about your Easter bonnet

01:06:38.470 --> 01:06:44.960
And of the girl I'm taking to the Easter

01:06:46.210 --> 01:06:59.040
I didn't exactly expect the welcome, Matt, but I thought somebody might say hello.

01:06:59.800 --> 01:06:59.840
Hello?

01:07:00.000 --> 01:07:04.040
What brings you here on this bright and uninviting day?

01:07:04.470 --> 01:07:06.850
I've discovered something, my friends, about life.

01:07:07.930 --> 01:07:08.430
Meaning what?

01:07:09.290 --> 01:07:11.360
Well, I don't want success.

01:07:11.520 --> 01:07:14.730
I want the true happiness you people have found here at the inn.

01:07:15.540 --> 01:07:16.740
You're not going to stay in the inn.

01:07:17.240 --> 01:07:18.000
Not just stay.

01:07:18.140 --> 01:07:20.360
I want to be part of your shows, help you in your work,

01:07:21.110 --> 01:07:22.610
share your simple pleasures.

01:07:23.470 --> 01:07:25.190
I asked you once not to interfere, Ted.

01:07:25.730 --> 01:07:28.290
Please believe me, I'm a tired, lonely, and unhappy man.

01:07:29.020 --> 01:07:29.940
But I could be happy...

01:07:30.000 --> 01:07:31.980
helping the two people I like the best.

01:07:33.150 --> 01:07:33.890
Will you take me in?

01:07:34.060 --> 01:07:36.360
My motherly intuition tells me to throw him out.

01:07:37.260 --> 01:07:38.720
At least give him the benefit of the doubt.

01:07:39.440 --> 01:07:40.640
I'm giving him plenty of doubt.

01:07:41.640 --> 01:07:44.440
Are you kidding with that sharing life's simple pleasures?

01:07:45.980 --> 01:07:47.140
May I go inside with you?

01:07:47.580 --> 01:07:48.100
Of course.

01:07:49.860 --> 01:07:51.560
My trunks will arrive this afternoon.

01:07:51.860 --> 01:07:53.480
What do I do? Move in the broom closet?

01:07:53.640 --> 01:07:55.780
Jim, that's no way to talk to a man who's here to help you.

01:07:56.180 --> 01:07:57.220
The world doesn't change.

01:07:57.900 --> 01:07:59.860
A gentle smile often breeds a kick in the pants.

01:08:00.670 --> 01:08:02.680
But for your sake, Linda, I'll be big.

01:08:03.830 --> 01:08:25.320
I'll give you a tip about these things, Gus.

01:08:25.420 --> 01:08:27.200
They'll go up and back, but not sideways.

01:08:27.540 --> 01:08:29.920
Yeah, well, I keep forgetting this plane.

01:08:30.030 --> 01:08:31.510
King can't see where it's going.

01:08:31.690 --> 01:08:33.510
Yeah, we'll unload the rest of this stuff in the back, huh?

01:08:43.550 --> 01:08:44.870
What'd you do, get up before breakfast?

01:08:45.110 --> 01:08:45.750
Oh, every morning.

01:08:46.050 --> 01:08:46.950
First you slept well.

01:08:47.050 --> 01:08:48.070
When I found out how late you got in,

01:08:48.150 --> 01:08:49.230
I told Mamie to let you sleep.

01:08:50.020 --> 01:08:50.920
Life on a farm.

01:08:51.060 --> 01:08:51.760
Can't beat it, huh?

01:08:52.100 --> 01:08:53.600
Jim, you've made me very happy.

01:08:53.720 --> 01:08:54.320
That's fine.

01:08:54.760 --> 01:08:55.980
Now, how about you making me happy?

01:08:56.630 --> 01:08:58.510
You sound like a landlord with eviction papers.

01:08:58.870 --> 01:08:59.830
Oh, this is good news.

01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:02.100
Mila's back in New York. I got a letter from her yesterday.

01:09:02.940 --> 01:09:03.820
What happened to her millionaire?

01:09:04.370 --> 01:09:07.560
Slight mistake there. He didn't own millions, he owed them.

01:09:08.830 --> 01:09:09.350
Poor girl.

01:09:09.870 --> 01:09:12.370
Always straying to greener pastures and finding spinach.

01:09:12.650 --> 01:09:12.750
Yeah.

01:09:12.950 --> 01:09:15.750
Say, she was wondering if you'd be interested in taking her back as a partner.

01:09:16.220 --> 01:09:17.200
I think it'd be a great idea.

01:09:17.940 --> 01:09:18.860
Naturally, you would.

01:09:19.310 --> 01:09:21.210
But I like it here, with you and Linda.

01:09:21.620 --> 01:09:23.260
Yes, and we love having you, too.

01:09:24.870 --> 01:09:25.730
When are you leaving?

01:09:40.110 --> 01:09:40.910
I didn't just say something.

01:09:41.090 --> 01:09:42.010
You look so silly.

01:09:42.250 --> 01:09:42.710
Where's Jim?

01:09:43.500 --> 01:09:43.800
Inside.

01:09:44.040 --> 01:09:44.180
Good.

01:09:44.660 --> 01:09:45.260
I fixed it.

01:09:45.760 --> 01:09:47.340
Here's the news in one luscious word.

01:09:47.780 --> 01:09:48.140
Hollywood.

01:09:48.790 --> 01:09:51.050
Now, I told you I'm not leaving here until Linda goes with me.

01:09:51.260 --> 01:09:53.440
But this is the setup you needed to get her away from Jim.

01:09:53.820 --> 01:09:56.080
Now, there are going to be two Hollywood men here tonight to see the show.

01:09:56.220 --> 01:09:57.320
One's an important director.

01:09:57.820 --> 01:09:59.980
If they like your dancing, you and Linda...

01:10:00.000 --> 01:10:01.800
Linda will be on a westbound train tomorrow.

01:10:02.600 --> 01:10:03.980
We'd better find out if Linda's interested.

01:10:04.490 --> 01:10:04.910
No, no, no.

01:10:05.010 --> 01:10:07.590
We let her know when there's a contract staring her in the face.

01:10:07.690 --> 01:10:07.830
Look.

01:10:08.220 --> 01:10:09.740
I know you're in love with the girl,

01:10:09.800 --> 01:10:11.320
but forget it until we get her away from here.

01:10:11.580 --> 01:10:12.820
This is no time to be honest.

01:10:13.130 --> 01:10:14.090
Well, what should I do?

01:10:14.380 --> 01:10:16.280
All we have to do is to convince Jim

01:10:16.280 --> 01:10:19.040
that he'd be a heel if he stood in the way of a chance like this.

01:10:19.360 --> 01:10:20.080
Oh, that'll be easy.

01:10:20.700 --> 01:10:21.600
Like peeling a turtle.

01:10:31.280 --> 01:10:32.540
Remember, it says these go up here.

01:10:32.700 --> 01:10:33.460
Yeah, set them right down.

01:10:37.240 --> 01:10:39.780
Say, Gus, how'd you like to earn a slow $10?

01:10:40.720 --> 01:10:42.980
Oh, I don't care how slow, but sure.

01:10:43.400 --> 01:10:44.360
It's sure, all right.

01:10:44.980 --> 01:10:45.560
Here's the wrinkle.

01:10:45.880 --> 01:10:47.140
I want you to go down to the station,

01:10:47.530 --> 01:10:49.390
pick up a party, and start for Holiday Inn,

01:10:49.520 --> 01:10:50.380
but never get here.

01:10:50.680 --> 01:10:51.320
Could you handle that?

01:10:51.770 --> 01:10:52.470
Wouldn't be surprised.

01:10:53.240 --> 01:10:53.420
Hello?

01:10:54.000 --> 01:10:54.720
Long distance.

01:10:55.800 --> 01:10:57.380
That's what I want you to do with Linda Mason.

01:10:57.940 --> 01:10:58.640
Miss Mason?

01:10:59.050 --> 01:10:59.750
Our friend?

01:11:00.320 --> 01:11:01.760
You're not supposed to understand it, Gus.

01:11:02.680 --> 01:11:04.880
For that kind of money, you ought to be able to go by wearing a medicine hat.

01:11:06.560 --> 01:11:08.040
Hello? Yeah, just a minute.

01:11:11.680 --> 01:11:12.280
Long distance.

01:11:12.280 --> 01:11:17.410
I want to get Parkway Hotel, New York City, Miss Lila Dixon.

01:11:39.990 --> 01:11:42.530
Did Linda say she'd be here for final rehearsal?

01:11:42.750 --> 01:11:46.200
Oh, relax. Our audiences aren't professional critics.

01:12:02.880 --> 01:12:04.040
Gosh, you made a wrong turn.

01:12:04.910 --> 01:12:12.420
Shortcut. Shortcut to the shortcut.

01:12:30.830 --> 01:12:32.730
How could you possibly expect to drive through this?

01:12:33.030 --> 01:12:35.170
Well, I never had no trouble with a horse.

01:12:38.920 --> 01:12:41.540
Well, you'd better carry me to shore and I'll walk back to the highway.

01:12:42.160 --> 01:12:44.920
Well, I think you'd be better off waiting right here.

01:12:45.320 --> 01:12:46.920
Gus, will you please do as I say?

01:12:49.130 --> 01:12:58.280
Uh-huh.

01:13:12.540 --> 01:13:13.340
You pushed me.

01:13:13.400 --> 01:13:22.500
I swear the show will start any minute now.

01:13:22.980 --> 01:13:24.020
You said that an hour ago.

01:13:25.200 --> 01:13:26.740
Yeah, but this time I'm sincere.

01:13:28.000 --> 01:13:28.560
Excuse me.

01:13:53.070 --> 01:13:55.120
the show. You're on.

01:13:55.280 --> 01:13:57.640
What about Ted's partner? You've kept this crowd waiting

01:13:57.640 --> 01:13:59.770
long enough. He can go on without her. Have you gone nuts?

01:14:00.000 --> 01:14:00.940
rehearse the double dance.

01:14:30.060 --> 01:14:31.820
It's hotter than a firecracker.

01:14:32.090 --> 01:14:36.790
Don't need any long speeches or shouts of hooray.

01:14:37.390 --> 01:14:41.330
No words can say as much as firecrackers can say.

01:14:47.440 --> 01:14:59.300
Freedom, freedom on this day of independence.

01:15:00.090 --> 01:15:06.490
On this Independence Day, listen to an American troubadour from the USA.

01:15:08.520 --> 01:15:17.300
I'm singing a song of freedom for all people who cry out to be free.

01:15:19.840 --> 01:15:25.080
Free to sail the seven seas, free to worship as we please.

01:15:25.140 --> 01:15:29.940
If the birds up in the trees can be free, why can't we?

01:15:30.000 --> 01:15:40.370
Sing a song of freedom to all people wherever they may be.

01:15:40.910 --> 01:15:48.380
Free to speak and free to hear, free from wanting, free from fear.

01:15:48.790 --> 01:15:58.390
Sons of freedom, far and near who agree, sing with me that all God's people shall be free.

01:16:01.940 --> 01:16:17.130
Free to sail the seven seas, free to worship as we please.

01:16:17.650 --> 01:16:25.640
If the birds up in the trees can be free, I can't breathe, bringing us on up.

01:16:30.720 --> 01:16:36.650
Free to speak and free to hear

01:16:36.650 --> 01:16:39.510
Free from want and free from fear

01:16:39.510 --> 01:16:42.910
Sons of freedom, far and near who agree

01:16:42.910 --> 01:16:44.400
Sing with me

01:16:44.400 --> 01:16:49.480
That all God's people shall be free

01:17:06.430 --> 01:17:07.250
Will you give me a laugh?

01:17:07.450 --> 01:17:08.230
Sure, hop in.

01:17:16.470 --> 01:17:18.690
Aren't you Ted Hanover's former dancing partner?

01:17:20.090 --> 01:17:23.400
Yes, although I wouldn't exactly say former.

01:17:23.970 --> 01:17:25.610
I'm dancing with him at the inn tonight.

01:17:27.060 --> 01:17:29.970
But I... doesn't he have a new partner?

01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:31.620
Oh, she won't be there tonight.

01:17:33.430 --> 01:17:34.390
I didn't know that.

01:17:35.690 --> 01:17:36.970
I work at the inn.

01:17:39.370 --> 01:17:39.730
Waitress?

01:17:41.500 --> 01:17:41.860
Yes.

01:17:43.410 --> 01:17:45.490
I know your boss, Jim Hardy, quite well.

01:17:46.560 --> 01:17:47.080
Quite well?

01:17:48.290 --> 01:17:51.030
Then he's responsible for your rejoining Mr. Hanover.

01:17:51.640 --> 01:17:51.980
Uh-huh.

01:17:53.120 --> 01:17:55.940
And by the way, if I were you, I'd look my prettiest tonight when I'm waiting on table.

01:17:56.400 --> 01:17:59.660
Jim says there'll be a couple of men there from Hollywood to consider Ted and me for pictures.

01:18:00.990 --> 01:18:29.700
then mr hanover's other partner will be missing this chance to go to hollywood yes although she can't be very talented or they wouldn't be working at the inn ted and i played only the best places listen you're late for the show already if you'd care to let me drive i know a shortcut that'll get us there fifteen minutes sooner there's a farmhouse near here and i'll have us towed out in a couple of minutes

01:18:30.000 --> 01:18:31.080
For the love of Mudd, hurry.

01:18:31.320 --> 01:18:32.140
Wait right here.

01:18:32.930 --> 01:18:34.070
What else can I do?

01:18:42.140 --> 01:18:42.740
You're on now.

01:18:43.380 --> 01:18:44.160
Linda isn't here yet.

01:18:44.300 --> 01:18:45.520
You've got to save the pieces.

01:18:45.680 --> 01:18:47.620
Keep those men interested now and do a number with Linda later.

01:18:48.190 --> 01:18:48.870
What can I do?

01:18:48.990 --> 01:18:49.910
Well, fake something.

01:18:51.380 --> 01:18:52.340
Fake something, Carlton.

01:18:59.120 --> 01:18:59.700
There's your cue.

01:19:00.640 --> 01:19:02.600
Don't fail me, keep them flying.

01:19:02.800 --> 01:19:03.620
I'll keep them flying.

01:20:01.400 --> 01:20:01.700
Thank you.

01:22:16.030 --> 01:22:16.550
What happened to you?

01:22:17.030 --> 01:22:18.350
Bad job of sabotage.

01:22:21.020 --> 01:22:21.580
Excuse me.

01:22:25.690 --> 01:22:28.890
Well, Jim, you deliberately kept me from working at the inn tonight, didn't you?

01:22:29.470 --> 01:22:29.630
Yeah.

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:33.160
You knew there would be men here from Hollywood who might offer me a chance in pictures.

01:22:33.890 --> 01:22:35.710
You decided I shouldn't have that opportunity.

01:22:36.310 --> 01:22:37.850
Not even the opportunity to refuse.

01:22:38.550 --> 01:22:41.750
I was afraid the offer might be too important for you to turn down.

01:22:42.130 --> 01:22:44.550
The point is you don't trust me to make my own decisions

01:22:44.550 --> 01:22:47.030
because they might interfere with your own selfish plans.

01:22:47.750 --> 01:22:49.250
I've had about enough of that, Jim.

01:22:50.920 --> 01:22:54.300
Ted, Linda, Mr. Parker, Mr. Dunbar,

01:22:54.740 --> 01:22:56.620
I want you to meet the greatest aunt's seamen in show business,

01:22:56.740 --> 01:22:59.090
Hanover and Mason, and the owner, Jim Hardy.

01:22:59.330 --> 01:22:59.970
Oh, glad to know.

01:23:00.000 --> 01:23:01.800
I know you, Hardy. Nice little place you've got here.

01:23:01.940 --> 01:23:04.660
Gentlemen, even though you haven't seen Miss Mason dance, I can assure you...

01:23:04.660 --> 01:23:08.290
Hardy, Hollywood is always interested in new ideas, and we think this is a honey.

01:23:08.470 --> 01:23:08.790
Thank you.

01:23:08.890 --> 01:23:11.010
Frankly, we'd like to do a picture based on Holiday Inn.

01:23:11.350 --> 01:23:13.930
The idea behind it, how it works, the special holiday songs.

01:23:14.250 --> 01:23:17.930
Of course, it's purely a speculative thing, far from foolproof, and we can't afford to pay too much.

01:23:18.320 --> 01:23:21.520
You don't have to start talking it down because the idea is not for sale.

01:23:22.230 --> 01:23:23.590
Well, maybe I haven't explained enough.

01:23:23.970 --> 01:23:26.330
We expect to use Mr. Hanover and his partner in the picture.

01:23:27.010 --> 01:23:29.980
Well, I don't know how the others feel, but I'd like to keep this...

01:23:30.000 --> 01:23:34.080
little setup just the way it is. Jim, would you be decent just once and let somebody else around here

01:23:34.080 --> 01:23:37.960
have a chance? Oh, wait a minute, Danny. After all, the place belongs to him. He can do as he wants.

01:23:38.180 --> 01:23:43.660
I guess it was just too good to last, huh? A simple little layout where we could do our best at the

01:23:43.660 --> 01:23:49.210
work we know without having any illusions of glory. I can see now that I'm the only one who

01:23:49.210 --> 01:23:54.420
could be happy here. Go ahead. Take the idea. Take the music. Take Linda. Take the whole darn thing.

01:23:54.610 --> 01:23:59.320
But what about you? We'll need you and Hollywood to write the rest of the music. I work right here.

01:24:00.000 --> 01:24:07.760
send you the music when it's written. And don't bother me before, huh? Guess maybe I was a little

01:24:07.760 --> 01:24:15.730
selfish, huh? Is that the deal you wanted or should I have thrown in my shirt? Chummy's sort of a

01:24:15.730 --> 01:24:22.440
fella, isn't he? Listen, Linda, if you really want to stay here, don't talk that way. This is the chance

01:24:22.440 --> 01:24:26.700
you wanted, isn't it? Of course! Boy, are we happy!

01:27:05.310 --> 01:27:06.850
Happy Thanksgiving, Mr. Jim.

01:27:07.270 --> 01:27:09.830
Same to you, Mamie, and staff.

01:27:10.370 --> 01:27:12.470
Didn't I tell you children to stay in the kitchen?

01:27:12.690 --> 01:27:14.630
Those wings ain't gonna fly away.

01:27:14.830 --> 01:27:15.830
Now, shoot, get.

01:27:18.060 --> 01:27:19.760
Everything's ready and hot, Mr. Jim.

01:27:20.000 --> 01:27:20.680
Thank you, Mamie.

01:27:42.090 --> 01:27:44.720
I've got plenty to be thankful for.

01:27:45.700 --> 01:27:46.300
Are you kidding?

01:27:47.390 --> 01:27:52.720
I haven't got a great big yacht to sail from shore to shore.

01:27:53.790 --> 01:27:56.830
Still, I've got plenty to be thankful for.

01:27:58.000 --> 01:27:58.720
Load it, Dad.

01:28:00.000 --> 01:28:03.260
I've got plenty to be thankful for.

01:28:03.880 --> 01:28:04.480
Like what?

01:28:05.420 --> 01:28:10.940
No private car, no caviar, no carpet on my floor.

01:28:12.120 --> 01:28:14.940
Still, I've got plenty to be thankful for.

01:28:15.460 --> 01:28:17.480
You know you're better off than I am.

01:28:17.580 --> 01:28:19.610
I've got eyes to see with.

01:28:19.810 --> 01:28:20.740
You need glasses.

01:28:20.900 --> 01:28:22.480
Ears to hear with.

01:28:23.290 --> 01:28:23.790
Fly with.

01:28:23.830 --> 01:28:26.830
Arms to hug with, lips to kiss with.

01:28:27.240 --> 01:28:28.580
Someone to adore.

01:28:29.140 --> 01:28:29.840
You're a little flat.

01:28:30.000 --> 01:28:40.130
too. How could anybody ask more? My needs are small. I buy them all at the five and ten

01:28:40.130 --> 01:28:56.880
cent store. Sing it. Sing it pretty. Why, you ain't at a bite. Poutin' maybe. Who is

01:28:56.880 --> 01:28:59.550
this? That's Mr. Jones. Jonesy?

01:29:00.220 --> 01:29:01.800
I'm sorry. I knew him too well.

01:29:02.230 --> 01:29:03.630
But you've got to eat.

01:29:03.830 --> 01:29:06.230
The trouble ain't with that turkey, Mr. Jim.

01:29:06.430 --> 01:29:07.210
It's you.

01:29:07.960 --> 01:29:10.290
I feel all right. I'm riding high, baby.

01:29:10.900 --> 01:29:12.240
Well, why you close the inn

01:29:12.240 --> 01:29:14.580
and sit around like a jellyfish with the misery?

01:29:14.930 --> 01:29:16.870
Because a slicker stole your gal

01:29:16.870 --> 01:29:19.710
and you ain't got fight enough to get her back.

01:29:20.860 --> 01:29:23.240
Oh, excuse me, Mr. Jim, but...

01:29:23.240 --> 01:29:24.460
Well, I tried to keep her here.

01:29:24.900 --> 01:29:26.720
What kind of keeping is that?

01:29:27.090 --> 01:29:28.070
Nothing but tricks.

01:29:28.510 --> 01:29:29.970
If you went to Hollywood...

01:29:30.000 --> 01:29:33.400
and told Miss Linda how much you loves her and misses her

01:29:33.400 --> 01:29:36.660
and told her that the way a lady likes to hear it told.

01:29:37.160 --> 01:29:41.620
I'll bet you she'd be the quickest ex-movie star that ever exed.

01:29:43.010 --> 01:29:44.030
You're crazy, baby.

01:29:44.690 --> 01:29:45.830
I'm crazy.

01:29:47.120 --> 01:29:48.480
I knows Miss Linda.

01:29:49.110 --> 01:29:51.690
I knows her like I knows my own kids.

01:29:52.630 --> 01:29:55.250
Why, she ain't the fancy type no more than you are.

01:29:56.210 --> 01:29:59.290
What she wants is what you got right here.

01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:03.170
that woman has to have them things told to them the right way.

01:30:03.950 --> 01:30:06.630
You could melt her heart right down to butter

01:30:06.630 --> 01:30:09.180
if you'd only turn on the heat.

01:30:10.580 --> 01:30:13.970
Maybe you don't try to take a fellow's gal away from him

01:30:14.030 --> 01:30:19.570
after he's bought the ring, as I recall, do you?

01:30:20.160 --> 01:30:21.660
Now you're a chicken.

01:30:22.200 --> 01:30:24.780
Sure, woman has to be told things the right way.

01:30:25.080 --> 01:30:25.980
Yes, sir.

01:30:39.560 --> 01:30:42.670
the night I've been dreaming about actually here.

01:30:43.010 --> 01:30:44.390
This is still my wedding, you know.

01:30:44.670 --> 01:30:45.770
You make me feel like a kibitzer.

01:30:46.090 --> 01:30:47.070
Now, don't misunderstand me.

01:30:47.110 --> 01:30:49.050
I'm happy because this marriage means

01:30:49.050 --> 01:30:51.390
that we can all settle down and stop worrying.

01:30:51.550 --> 01:30:53.780
I wish I had your confidence without your viewpoint.

01:30:54.310 --> 01:30:56.090
My fingers are crossed until Linda and I

01:30:56.090 --> 01:30:57.570
are on that plane bound for Yuma.

01:30:57.910 --> 01:30:58.930
Now, what's worrying you?

01:30:59.370 --> 01:30:59.970
I don't know, except...

01:31:00.120 --> 01:31:04.860
I've been this close to marriage before, only to wake up next morning and find myself with no bride and a hangover.

01:31:05.060 --> 01:31:08.560
Look, the girl said yes. The picture finishes tonight. There's a judge waiting in Yuma.

01:31:09.480 --> 01:31:13.540
Come in. Everything is all set and ready. What could possibly happen to...

01:31:16.150 --> 01:31:16.670
Hiya, fellas.

01:31:19.900 --> 01:31:22.500
Jim, what brought you here?

01:31:22.720 --> 01:31:23.100
A train?

01:31:23.400 --> 01:31:24.180
A chug-chug-chug-chug?

01:31:25.060 --> 01:31:25.500
Wedding?

01:31:25.660 --> 01:31:26.180
When is it?

01:31:26.920 --> 01:31:27.240
Wedding?

01:31:27.380 --> 01:31:27.560
Yeah.

01:31:28.220 --> 01:31:29.680
Uh, well, we...

01:31:30.000 --> 01:31:31.240
I hadn't said any exact time.

01:31:31.540 --> 01:31:32.520
Have you seen Linda?

01:31:32.720 --> 01:31:33.900
No, no, not yet.

01:31:34.020 --> 01:31:35.200
But, say, I saw your director.

01:31:35.340 --> 01:31:36.880
He told me he was shooting the finale tonight.

01:31:37.530 --> 01:31:38.850
I thought I'd like to see how you make pictures.

01:31:40.050 --> 01:31:40.770
He wouldn't...

01:31:40.770 --> 01:31:42.410
You wouldn't like what they're doing tonight.

01:31:42.630 --> 01:31:42.990
Why not?

01:31:43.110 --> 01:31:45.510
Oh, no, that's dull, technical style.

01:31:45.690 --> 01:31:47.170
I'm a dull, technical sort of a fella.

01:31:47.730 --> 01:31:49.970
Perhaps if you'd wait and see Linda tomorrow.

01:31:50.290 --> 01:31:52.470
Oh, no, I want to see the finish.

01:31:53.020 --> 01:31:55.680
The success of you and Linda means a lot to me, pal.

01:31:56.770 --> 01:31:58.150
So why don't you be yourself?

01:31:58.350 --> 01:31:59.050
What are you up to?

01:32:00.860 --> 01:32:02.260
Well, I'm a son of a gun.

01:32:02.690 --> 01:32:05.450
This is a beautiful hunk of welcome for a guy who comes coast to coast

01:32:05.450 --> 01:32:08.030
just to wish you a Merry Christmas and a happy wedding.

01:32:08.730 --> 01:32:13.150
You remember how I suspected you when you came to live at the inn on Easter morning?

01:32:14.250 --> 01:32:15.050
Silly, wasn't it?

01:32:15.210 --> 01:32:16.550
Now I know he's up to something.

01:32:16.770 --> 01:32:18.470
Oh, wait a minute now. Let's not be unfair.

01:32:19.010 --> 01:32:21.730
Now, we're treating Jim like a poor country cousin.

01:32:21.750 --> 01:32:22.730
He doesn't mean any harm.

01:32:23.010 --> 01:32:25.010
No, he just wants to see Linda.

01:32:25.150 --> 01:32:26.630
Let's show him Linda.

01:32:27.630 --> 01:32:29.150
Goodwill on earth toward men.

01:32:29.390 --> 01:32:29.970
Is this the way...

01:32:30.000 --> 01:32:34.380
What's this? Hey, Ted, what is this?

01:32:35.870 --> 01:32:36.970
I was afraid you'd gone crazy.

01:32:37.560 --> 01:32:39.700
I'll keep him in here till you get Linda on that plane.

01:32:43.170 --> 01:32:44.430
I'd better hurry and get my clothes on.

01:32:44.620 --> 01:32:47.040
In the meantime, I'll go down to the set and see how near ready they are.

01:32:47.480 --> 01:32:48.940
Wait a minute. My clothes are in there.

01:32:49.140 --> 01:32:51.900
Merry Christmas! Jim! Hal!

01:32:52.100 --> 01:32:54.650
Wait! Stop! We were only fooling!

01:32:56.350 --> 01:32:57.830
Only you could think of a thing like that.

01:33:05.560 --> 01:33:06.080
Who are you calling?

01:33:07.470 --> 01:33:09.800
Nobody. The operator's gone.

01:33:43.090 --> 01:33:53.390
It's one of the most authentic reproduction jobs we've ever done.

01:33:53.940 --> 01:33:56.960
And all worked out from those photographs we took of your place in Connecticut.

01:34:00.570 --> 01:34:03.570
Well, Mamie and the kids ought to see that they'd never believe it.

01:34:04.260 --> 01:34:04.740
Anything wrong?

01:34:06.070 --> 01:34:07.910
Well, that Christmas tree's a little out of place.

01:34:08.490 --> 01:34:11.400
I guess nobody would notice that but me or Linda.

01:34:12.060 --> 01:34:13.460
We're going to start rolling in a couple of minutes.

01:34:13.860 --> 01:34:15.260
Come along with me where you can see everything.

01:34:15.340 --> 01:34:16.880
No, I'll just sort of stay in the background.

01:34:16.940 --> 01:34:17.780
I don't want to get in your way.

01:34:18.200 --> 01:34:18.880
Well, suit yourself.

01:34:19.550 --> 01:34:20.130
I'll see you later.

01:34:20.290 --> 01:34:20.490
Right.

01:34:41.290 --> 01:34:43.890
All right, darling, we're going to follow you on the boom from here inside the inn.

01:34:44.470 --> 01:34:46.130
And when you get in the other set, do your songs.

01:34:47.260 --> 01:34:48.640
Let's see, I think you have the mood.

01:34:49.060 --> 01:34:50.600
Your Hollywood success was empty.

01:34:50.930 --> 01:34:52.370
You've lost the one man you love.

01:34:52.960 --> 01:34:54.200
You know, the usual hope.

01:34:55.220 --> 01:34:57.480
Just make me cry and you can get to that wedding.

01:34:58.130 --> 01:34:58.870
I'm ready for rehearsal.

01:34:59.030 --> 01:34:59.330
Please.

01:35:00.320 --> 01:35:01.040
Let's shoot it.

01:35:01.370 --> 01:35:02.610
Okay. It's a take.

01:35:07.540 --> 01:35:09.780
All right, everybody, quiet on the stage. It's a take.

01:35:10.820 --> 01:35:14.150
Close them up. They're quiet down.

01:35:14.390 --> 01:35:15.490
Let's get settled, everybody.

01:35:19.270 --> 01:35:20.910
Come on, everybody, let's get settled now.

01:35:21.360 --> 01:35:21.860
It's a picture.

01:35:22.640 --> 01:35:23.420
Get out there with your bro.

01:35:24.600 --> 01:35:25.280
Hit your snow.

01:35:36.270 --> 01:35:40.090
Sorry, Mr. Hannibal, but when the red light's on, you couldn't get in even if you owned the studio.

01:35:40.410 --> 01:35:41.470
Oh, but, Pop, this is important.

01:35:41.570 --> 01:35:42.810
I know. So is the light.

01:35:43.070 --> 01:35:44.630
Hit your playback. Music!

01:36:31.660 --> 01:36:31.860
Great.

01:37:31.790 --> 01:37:40.390
He'll drown this, he lay bells in the snow.

01:38:01.920 --> 01:38:08.460
May your days carry and brine.

01:38:18.000 --> 01:38:25.310
How could he get that far in five minutes?

01:38:26.090 --> 01:38:27.190
The lady must have been willing.

01:38:28.320 --> 01:38:29.960
But the world can't do this to her.

01:38:30.000 --> 01:38:58.040
Here she comes down the street. I'll admit my defeat. I've won my hot toddy over my scarred body.

01:39:00.000 --> 01:39:07.530
I knew that I'd win singing, but wait until she gets a load of your dancing.

01:39:09.520 --> 01:39:14.810
We stay at the end singing.

01:39:16.170 --> 01:39:18.590
All by myself, I'll have to stick to my dancing.

01:39:24.010 --> 01:39:27.230
I'm here to end your dancing trouble and strife.

01:39:27.410 --> 01:39:29.890
Oh, this will be fun, Miss Hitton.

01:39:30.000 --> 01:39:49.690
run has come back into my life. We'll stay at the end. We'll have to begin dancing. We've each

01:39:49.690 --> 01:39:59.920
other to cling to. You'll be easy to sing to. And you're easy to dance with. So let the old

01:40:00.000 --> 01:40:03.360
You die with a fine goodbye
